  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington is firing on all cylinders while Hicksville is signaling a deeper structural problem that needs your attention.\n\nPort Washington delivered 27% revenue growth yesterday on 6 active groomers, hitting $532 per groomer\u2014well above the 30-day baseline of $505. This is real operational excellence: core grooms up 23%, add-on attach improving to 41%, and retail exploding 64% on transaction count up 66%. Week-to-date momentum is strong (up 21%), and the month is tracking slightly ahead of DOW-adjusted expectation (+1.7%). You should be proud of this team's execution. The 7.2 bather hours yesterday (vs. a 5.2h trailing average) signals they're properly staffed to handle volume without bottlenecks. Inventory is tight on bestsellers\u2014X-Small Treat Tables and bully sticks are at zero\u2014but nothing critical.\n\nHicksville is a different story. Yesterday's 35% revenue drop to just $783 on only 2 groomers producing $310 per groomer is a capacity crisis masquerading as a sales problem. With zero scheduled bather hours and no grooming lift coming, this location is structurally under-resourced. The 12+ week visit-gap bucket grew from 8.4% to 10.2%\u2014that's stealth churn, Kyle. Customers are stretching out their appointments or moving elsewhere. Month-to-date performance is up 5.4% DOW-adjusted, which masks the fact that you're running 2 groomers instead of the 3\u20134 Port Washington deploys. The lapse pool of 58 customers ($39,960 annual value) is reactivatable, but not with current coverage.\n\nPort Washington: 5 groomers, 7.0h bathers today; 6 groomers, 7.0h bathers tomorrow; 29 groomer-days across next 7 days. Hicksville: 2 groomers, 0.0h bathers today and tomorrow; 11 groomer-days over next 7 days."
